          "title": "You'll want to know: гавань",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "гавань (gávan) — \"a harbour\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Вечером в гавань вернулись все лодки. Vécherom v gávan vernúlis vse lódki. In the evening all the boats came back to the harbour."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine, though it ends in -ь."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "гавань (gávan) was borrowed from Dutch haven 'a harbour' (EtymDB), from Middle Dutch havene."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
