          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "маяк (mayák) is usually traced to a Turkic word for a pole or a marker. EtymDB lists the Russian word with the sense 'lighthouse' but no source, so the line is hedged."
            }
          ]
        },
